---
import { url } from '@/lib/url';
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'About LabelsCrop';
const description =
	'LabelsCrop is a free, browser-only toolkit for Indian e-commerce sellers: crop and sort shipping labels for printing, and work out your real profit from the marketplace payment file — no login, no uploads, no watermarks.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
		<h1 data-reveal class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">About LabelsCrop</h1>

		<div data-reveal class="prose prose-neutral mt-8 max-w-none text-muted-foreground dark:prose-invert">
			<p>
				LabelsCrop exists because running a Meesho shop means doing two thankless jobs over and over.
				The first is getting orders out of the door: Meesho — like most Indian marketplaces — exports
				shipping labels with a tax invoice glued to the same page, in whatever order your orders
				happened to sync in. The second is finding out whether any of it made money, which the
				supplier panel will not tell you: it reports what it paid you, and stops there.
			</p>
			<p>So there are two tools, for the two ends of the same order:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong><a href={url('/tools/meesho-label-cropper')}>The label cropper</a></strong> crops the
					invoice away, fits the label to your printer, and sorts the batch the way you actually pack —
					with a pick list of how many of each SKU to pull off the shelf.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong><a href={url('/tools/meesho-profit-calculator')}>The profit calculator</a></strong>
					reads your payment file and works out what you really earned — after cost of goods, ads,
					returns and the rent and salaries no marketplace has ever heard of — down to the margin on
					each individual SKU.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>A few things we think matter enough to say plainly:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Nothing you add leaves your device.</strong> There is no server that processes your
					files. Cropping, sorting, PDF building and every profit calculation happen locally in your
					browser, using code that runs on your machine — not ours. That matters twice over here:
					one file holds your customers' addresses, the other holds your entire revenue.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>No account, ever.</strong> There's nothing to sign up for and nothing to forget
					a password for. Open a tool, use it, close the tab.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Free forever, funded by ads.</strong> Advertising is placed away from the upload,
					preview, and download flow, so it never gets in the way of actually getting the work done.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Both tools start with Meesho. Support for other marketplaces is on the roadmap — see the
				<a href={url('/faq')}>FAQ</a> for details.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div data-reveal class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-stretch justify-center gap-2.5 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
			<a
				href={url('/tools/meesho-label-cropper')}
				class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-primary px-6 text-base font-semibold text-primary-foreground shadow-sm transition-transform duration-150 hover:scale-[1.02] active:scale-[0.98]"
			>
				Open the Label Cropper
			</a>
			<a
				href={url('/tools/meesho-profit-calculator')}
				class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-border bg-background px-6 text-base font-semibold transition-colors hover:border-primary/40 hover:text-primary"
			>
				Open the Profit Calculator
			</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
